{{!
    @template enrol_apply/review_enrolments

    "Already in this course": the applicant's other enrolments in the course, through any
    enrolment method (docs/design/applicant-group-choice.md, C-D5), so a decider reads before the
    decision that the person is, say, already a student in one group by a key. Rendered only when
    there is one. A card of the left column, like the rules above it; each entry is the method in
    bold with its status as a badge, then the facts the record holds.

    The method's name and the role names arrive ESCAPED and are triple stashed: the enrolment
    method's and the role's own helpers return a mixed spelling, which the renderer normalises to
    the escaped one. The groups and the admission line are plain and double stashed. Each label
    and its value stay on one line, because a Behat "I should see" matches the raw text.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * hasenrolments boolean - whether the applicant holds any other enrolment in the course
    * enrolmentsheading string - the card's heading
    * enrolmentsrolelabel, enrolmentsgroupslabel, enrolmentsadmissionlabel string - the facts' labels
    * enrolments array - one entry per other enrolment, in the course's method order, each with
      method (ESCAPED), status (plain), statusclass (a literal background and text colour pair),
      hasfacts, hasrole, role (ESCAPED, comma-separated), hasgroups, groups (plain, the groups
      joined through that method this reader may see), hasadmission and admission (plain)
    * hasotherroles boolean, otherroleslabel string, otherroles string (ESCAPED) - roles held in
      the course outside any method, which no entry can be credited with

    Example context (json):
    {
        "hasenrolments": true,
        "enrolmentsheading": "Already in this course",
        "enrolmentsrolelabel": "Role",
        "enrolmentsgroupslabel": "Groups joined",
        "enrolmentsadmissionlabel": "Admitted",
        "enrolments": [
            {
                "method": "Apply as a student", "status": "Active", "statusclass": "bg-success text-white",
                "hasfacts": true, "hasrole": true, "role": "Student", "hasgroups": true, "groups": "Evening A",
                "hasadmission": true, "admission": "By the enrolment key of Evening A"
            }
        ],
        "hasotherroles": false,
        "otherroleslabel": "Also holds in this course",
        "otherroles": ""
    }
}}
{{#hasenrolments}}
<section class="enrol_apply-enrolments enrol_apply-box" aria-labelledby="enrol_apply_enrolments_heading" data-region="review-enrolments">
    <h2 class="enrol_apply-blocktitle" id="enrol_apply_enrolments_heading">{{enrolmentsheading}}</h2>
    <ul class="enrol_apply-timeline list-unstyled mb-0">
        {{#enrolments}}
            <li>
                <div class="enrol_apply-timelinehead">
                    <strong>{{{method}}}</strong>
                    <span class="badge {{statusclass}}">{{status}}</span>
                </div>
                {{#hasfacts}}
                    <dl class="enrol_apply-historyfacts mb-0">
                        {{#hasrole}}<div><dt>{{enrolmentsrolelabel}}</dt><dd>{{{role}}}</dd></div>{{/hasrole}}
                        {{#hasgroups}}<div><dt>{{enrolmentsgroupslabel}}</dt><dd>{{groups}}</dd></div>{{/hasgroups}}
                        {{#hasadmission}}<div><dt>{{enrolmentsadmissionlabel}}</dt><dd>{{admission}}</dd></div>{{/hasadmission}}
                    </dl>
                {{/hasfacts}}
            </li>
        {{/enrolments}}
    </ul>
    {{#hasotherroles}}
        <p class="enrol_apply-rulefact mb-0">{{#pix}}i/role, core{{/pix}}<span>{{otherroleslabel}}: {{{otherroles}}}</span></p>
    {{/hasotherroles}}
</section>
{{/hasenrolments}}
